 99%, rgba(255, 255, 255, 0) 100%);\r\n      background: -ms-radial-gradient(center, ellipse cover, rgba(247, 173, 148, 0.65) 0%, rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.01) 99%, rgba(255, 255, 255, 0) 100%);\r\n      background: radial-gradient(ellipse at center, rgba(247, 173, 148, 0.65) 0%, rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.01) 99%, rgba(255, 255, 255, 0) 100%);\r\n      filter: progid:DXImageTransform.Microsoft.gradient(startColorstr=\'#a6f7ad94\', endColorstr=\'#00ffffff\',GradientType=1 ); }\r\n\r\n.error-back {\r\n  text-decoration: none;\r\n  color: #430400;\r\n  font-size: 15px; }\r\n  .error-back:hover {\r\n    color: #EB957D;\r\n    text-shadow: 0 0 3px black; }\r\n\r\n</style>\r\n\r\n\r\n<html>\r\n<head>\r\n  <meta charset=\"utf-8\">\r\n  <meta http-equiv=\"X-UA-Compatible\" content=\"IE=edge,chrome=1\">\r\n	<title>404 Page no found</title>\r\n	<meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width\">\r\n  <!--[if gte IE 9]>\r\n	<style type=\"text/css\">\r\n		.gradient {\r\n		   filter: none;\r\n		}\r\n	</style>\r\n	<![endif]-->\r\n</head>\r\n<body>\r\n	<div class=\"error-page-wrap\">\r\n		<article class=\"error-page gradient\">\r\n			<hgroup>\r\n				<h1>403</h1>\r\n				<h2>oops! You don\'t have sufficient access. Please login to access this page</h2>\r\n			</hgroup>\r\n			<a href=\"<?php print $GLOBALS[\'base_url\']; ?>/home\" title=\"Back to site\" class=\"error-back\">back</a>\r\n		</article>\r\n	</div>\r\n</body>\r\n</html>',	'',	'php_code'),
('page',	0,	16,	16,	'und',	0,	'<p>Teachers/Professors/Students from educational institutions across the country can participate in the Lab Migration project. The participation procedure is different for college teachers and students.</p>\r\n\r\n<h4>For College Teachers:</h4>\r\n\r\n<ol>\r\n	<li>Fill the Lab Migration proposal form provided at <a href=\"https://cfd.fossee.in/lab-migration/proposal\">https://cfd.fossee.in/lab-migration/proposal</a>. To access the above mentioned page, please log in to the website. If you do not have a login account, please register <a href=\"http://cfd.fossee.in/user/register\">here</a>. In the proposal form provide details about your lab course, problem statements, titles of the exercises. Please provide a Problem Statement for each experiment&nbsp;proposed in a document format. To view the template of the document please <a href=\"https://cfd.fossee.in/sites/default/files/Problem_Statement_Template.doc\">click here.&nbsp;</a></li>\r\n	<li>In the proposal form, please indicate if you would like to submit the solution to the proposed problem. If you dont want to provide the solution, then it will be opened to the community. Anyone may come forward and provide the solution.</li>\r\n	<li>Once you have filled all the required fields, submit the form. On successful submission of the proposal form, you will receive a notification e-mail.</li>\r\n	<li>You will receive an approval/disapproval mail within few days. If you have chosen to submit the solution for the OpenFOAM cases by yourself, you can start solving examples in OpenFOAM for the assigned lab and upload the cases on the interface. To view the template for result submission please <a href=\"https://cfd.fossee.in/sites/default/files/Template_For_Result.doc\">click here</a>.&nbsp;</li>\r\n</ol>\r\n\r\n<p>Note:</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Any user who provides solutions for a lab course, can only work on one lab at a time. They can move on to another lab once the current lab\'s solutions have been provided.</p>\r\n\r\n<h4>For Students and other Community Members:</h4>\r\n\r\n<ol>\r\n	<li>Visit the page <a href=\"https://cfd.fossee.in/lab-migration/proposal\">https://cfd.fossee.in/lab-migration/open-proposal</a>. Please log in to access the above mentioned page. If you do not have a login account, please <a href=\"https://cfd.fossee.in/user/register\">click here</a> to create an account. This page will have a list of lab problems for which OpenFOAM cases are to be provided.</li>\r\n	<li>Select the lab for which you want to provide the solution. This you can do by clicking on the \"Apply\" button next to the \"Title of the Lab\". This action will take you to \"Lab Migration Solution Proposal\" form.</li>\r\n	<li>Once you submit the form, we will approve it taking into consideration your proposal and other proposals.</li>\r\n	<li>You will receive an email informing whether your proposal has been approved or disapproved. Once your proposal is approved, you can start solving examples in OpenFOAM for the assigned lab and upload the cases on the interface.&nbsp;To view the template for result submission please&nbsp;<a href=\"https://cfd.fossee.in/sites/default/files/Template_For_Result.doc\">click here</a>.&nbsp;</li>\r\n</ol>\r\n',	'',	'full_html'),
('page',	0,	17,	17,	'und',	0,	'<p><b>Submission guidelines :</b></p>\r\n\r\n<ol>\r\n	<li>Submit your case file in zip format. ( The case file should contain 0, constant,&nbsp;system folder,&nbsp;time step folders, Allrun file and a readme file. This will help the users to run the case easily.)</li>\r\n	<li>Also, send plots of velocity, pressure or any other variable mentioned in the problem.</li>\r\n	<li>Limit the size of your folder to maximum of 5 GB.</li>\r\n	<li>A document explaining description of the case set-up and the results should also be provided. To view the template of the document please <a href=\"https://cfd.fossee.in/sites/default/files/Template_For_Result_1.doc\">click here</a>.</li>\r\n</ol>\r\n',	'',	'filtered_html'),
('page',	0,	18,	18,	'und',	0,	'<div class=\"rtejustify\">\r\n<p>The FOSSEE Project has restarted the honorarium payment for Textbook Companion, Lab Migration, and the niche software activities like flowsheeting project, circuit simulation project, case study project, etc. The honorarium amount shall range from 1,500 - 5,000 INR as per the activity and the complexity of the work contributed.</p>\r\n<p>We shall continue to issue the e-certificate and give credits on our website for the contributions made. This policy will be effective for proposals accepted from Jan 2024. Please note that the FOSSEE project may change this policy in the future.</p>\r\n<p>Proposer - 1,500 INR\r\nHOD - 1,000 INR\r\nSolution provider - 300 per experiment (Min 5 experiments)\r\n</p>\r\n</div>',	'',	'full_html'),
('page',	0,	23,	23,	'und',	0,	'<p>Teachers/Professors/Students from educational institutions across the country can participate in the Lab Migration project. The participation procedure is different for college teachers and students.</p>\r\n\r\n<h4>For College Teachers:</h4>\r\n\r\n<ol>\r\n	<li>Fill the Lab Migration proposal form provided at <a href=\"http://cfd.fossee.in/lab-migration/proposal\">http://cfd.fossee.in/lab-migration/proposal</a>. To access the above mentioned page, please log in to the website. If you do not have a login account, please register here. In the proposal form provide details about your lab course, problem statements, titles of the exercises.</li>\r\n	<li>In the proposal form, choose between providing the OpenFOAM cases for the problems mentioned in the proposal form by yourself or floating the problems to the Lab Migration Project community.</li>\r\n	<li>In case you are not providing the OpenFOAM cases, other community members can propose to provide the OpenFOAM cases for the problems mentioned in your Lab Migration proposal.</li>\r\n	<li>While filling the proposal form, select whether you want the OpenFOAM cases of the problems mentioned in the proposal form to be made available for other members to view/download/use.</li>\r\n	<li>Once you have filled all the required fields, submit the form. On successful submission of the proposal form, you will receive a notification e-mail.</li>\r\n	<li>You will receive an approval/disapproval mail within few days. If you have chosen to submit the OpenFOAM cases yourself, you can start solving examples in OpenFOAM for the assigned lab and upload the cases on the interface.</li>\r\n</ol>\r\n\r\n<h4>For Students and other Community Members:</h4>\r\n\r\n<p>Note:</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Any user who provides solutions for a lab course, can only work on one lab at a time. They can move on to another lab once the current lab\'s solutions have been provided.</p>\r\n\r\n<ol>\r\n	<li>Visit the page <a href=\"http://cfd.fossee.in/lab-migration/open-proposal\">http://cfd.fossee.in/lab-migration/open-proposal</a>. Please log in to access the above mentioned page. If you do not have a login account, please <a href=\"http://cfd.fossee.in/user/register\">click here</a> to create an account. This page will have a list of lab problems for which OpenFOAM cases are to be provided.</li>\r\n	<li>Select the lab for which you want to provide the solution. This you can do by clicking on the \"Apply\" button next to the \"Title of the Lab\". This action will take you to \"Lab Migration Solution Proposal\" form.</li>\r\n	<li>Once you submit the form, we will approve it taking into consideration your proposal and other proposals.</li>\r\n	<li>You will receive an email informing whether your proposal has been approved or disapproved. Once your proposal is approved, you can start solving examples in OpenFOAM for the assigned lab and upload the cases on the interface.</li>\r\n</ol>\r\n',	'',	'full_html'),
('page',	0,	24,	24,	'und',	0,	'<p>The Textbook Companion Project ports solved examples from standard textbooks using OpenFOAM.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>To view Completed Books click <a href=\"https://cfd.fossee.in/textbook-companion/textbook-run\">here</a>. <strong>Please note that we are no longer accepting TBC proposals.</strong>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p>The Textbook Companion Project aims to improve documentation for OpenFOAM by making it easy for textbook users to start using OpenFOAM.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n',	'',	'full_html'),
('page',	0,	25,	25,	'und',	0,	'<p>1.&nbsp;&nbsp;Strictly use OpenFOAM-2.2.x and above for solving cases.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>2.&nbsp;&nbsp;The dependencies on other codes/functions (if any) should be mentioned as a comment clearly before starting the case.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>3.&nbsp;&nbsp;Do not include problem statement/text from the book in the case.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>4.&nbsp;&nbsp;All the outputs must be displayed in appropriate format (along with units mentioned).</p>\r\n\r\n<p>5.&nbsp;&nbsp;All the plots must have appropriate labels on its axes.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>6.&nbsp;&nbsp;Once you have completed solving the examples, mail us at <a href=\"mailto:cfd-tbc@fossee.in\" target=\"_blank\">cfd-tbc (at) fossee (dot) in</a> with complete details including your name and allotted book.</p>\r\n',	'',	'full_html'),
('page',	0,	26,	26,	'und',	0,	'<p>Work has been completed on the following books under the Textbook Companion Project</p>\r\n<span style=\"color:red;\">The list below is not the books as named but only are the solved example for CFD</span>\r\n<hr style=\"background-color: #abb2b8;\" />\r\n<?php\r\n\r\n$query = db_select(\'textbook_companion_preference\', \'pe\');\r\n$query->fields(\'pe\', array(\'id\',\'book\',\'author\'));\r\n$query->fields(\'po\', array(\'full_name\'));\r\n$query->fields(\'po\', array(\'university\'));\r\n$query->fields(\'po\', array(\'completion_date\'));\r\n$query->leftJoin(\'textbook_companion_proposal\', \'po\', \'pe.proposal_id = po.id\');\r\n$query->condition(\'po.proposal_status\', 3);\r\n$query->condition(\'pe.approval_status\', 1);\r\n$query->orderBy(\'po.completion_date\', \'DESC\');\r\n$preference_q = $query->execute();\r\necho \"<table>\";\r\necho \"<thead><th>Sl No</th><th>Title of the Book</th><th>Contributor Name</th><th>University / Institute</th><th>Year of Completion</th></thead>\";\r\n$i = 1;\r\n\r\nwhile ($preference_data = $preference_q->fetchObject()) {\r\n\r\n  echo \"<tr>\";\r\n echo \"<td>\";\r\necho($i);\r\n echo \"</td>\";\r\n  echo \"<td>\";\r\n  echo l($preference_data->book . \' by \' . $preference_data->author , \'textbook-companion/textbook-run/\' . $preference_data->id);\r\n  echo\"</td>\"; \r\n  echo \"<td>\";\r\n  echo($preference_data->full_name);\r\n  echo\"</td>\"; \r\n echo \"<td>\";\r\n  echo($preference_data->university);\r\n  echo\"</td>\"; \r\n echo \"<td>\";\r\n  echo(date(\"Y\", $preference_data->completion_date));\r\n  echo\"</td>\"; \r\n\r\n  echo \"</tr>\";\r\n$i++;\r\n}\r\necho \"</table>\";\r\n?>',	'',	'php_code'),
('page',	0,	27,	27,	'und',	0,	'<p>\r\n	Work has been completed on the following books under the Textbook Companion Project\r\n</p>\r\n<hr style=\"background-color: #abb2b8;\" />\r\n<?php\r\n\r\n$query = db_select(\'textbook_companion_preference\', \'pe\');\r\n$query->fields(\'pe\', array(\'book\', \'author\', \'publisher\', \'year\', \'id\'));\r\n$query->leftJoin(\'textbook_companion_proposal\', \'po\', \'pe.proposal_id = po.id\');\r\n$query->condition(\'po.proposal_status\', 3, \'<>\');\r\n$query->condition(\'pe.approval_status\', 1);\r\n$query->orderBy(\'pe.book\', \'ASC\');\r\n$preference_q = $query->execute();\r\n\r\necho \"<ol>\";\r\nwhile ($preference_data = $preference_q->fetchObject()) {\r\n  echo \"<li>\";\r\n  echo $preference_data->book . \" by \" . $preference_data->author . \", \" . $preference_data->publisher . \", \" . $preference_data->year;\r\n  echo \"</li>\";\r\n}\r\necho \"</ol>\";\r\n?>',	'',	'php_code'),
('page',	0,	28,	28,	'und',	0,	'<p><strong>1. What is Textbook Companion?</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p>The Textbook Companion aims to generate an online collection of OpenFOAM cases/solvers for worked out examples and select exercise problems from standard textbooks.</p>\r\n\r\n<hr />\r\n<p><strong>2. Which book can I choose?</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p>Any book containing more than 20 solved examples can be chosen for creating TBC. However, the applicant has to ensure that the proposed book has not already been completed or is being completed currently by any other intern. The list of completed books and books in progress is available on the website. In case the book has already been completed or is being worked upon by another intern, then the book proposal will be rejected. Also note that the responsibility of ensuring such a scenario does not arise bears with the intern and/or his teacher as per the undertaking form.</p>\r\n\r\n<hr />\r\n<p><strong>3. What is the minimum number of examples a book should have?</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p>Please make sure that the book proposed by you has at least 20 examples. If student is not able to find 20 examples in one book, then he/she can refer another book along with the existing book. But each book should have at least 10 examples. If it is found that the number of examples is less, the internship might be canceled during the later stages. Along with the book proposal, you are required to send a chapter\'s case file from one of the three proposed books to cfd-tbc (at) fossee (dot) in in a .zip or .tgz file. The subject for the mail with sample case should be \"New Book Proposal-Sample Cases-\".We will not contact you to send the case file. It is suggested that you propose the book as early as possible since your preferred book may be assigned to someone else.</p>\r\n\r\n<hr />\r\n<p><strong>4. Who is eligible for internship?</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p>Students pursuing graduation in mechanical, chemical, civil, aerospace from various colleges are eligible for this internship.</p>\r\n\r\n<hr />\r\n<p><strong>5. What are the prerequisites for applying for the internship?</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p>There are no prerequisites for applying for the internship. The student should be comfortable with environment of OpenFoam and should be aware of basic OpenFoam commands and operations.</p>\r\n\r\n<hr />\r\n<p><strong>6. What is the deadline for the internship?</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p>The internship should be completed within 3 months after proposing the book. The solved cases can be uploaded in multiple groups (e.g. chapter wise) before the deadline. Applicants may contact us at cfd-tbc (at) fossee (dot) in if the deadline needs to be changed. Please note that the extension of the deadline for the completion of the internship will be considered only in case of genuine reasons.</p>\r\n\r\n<hr />\r\n<p><strong>7. What is the last date of completing the internship?</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p>The internship should be completed within 3 months after proposing the book.</p>\r\n\r\n<hr />\r\n<p><strong>8. Can the internship be canceled if it is allotted to me? Has it ever been canceled for anybody?</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p>Yes. Refusal to meet the deadline, poor solving cases and badgering the OpenFOAM team are some of the reasons as to why the internship could be cancelled. No partial payment will be made in such a case.</p>\r\n\r\n<hr />\r\n<p><strong>9. Is it necessary to come to IIT Bombay for completing the internship?</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p>No. There is no need to come to IIT Bombay at any phase of the internship. All the correspondence will be carried out via e-mails and/or postal services.</p>\r\n\r\n<hr />\r\n<p><strong>10. Is it necessary to have a mentor?</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p>No. According to the new TBC policy effective Feb 1 2014, the student is not required to have a mentor.</p>\r\n\r\n<hr />\r\n<p><strong>11. Can I work on more than one book simultaneously?</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p>Yes. If a student is not able to find 10 examples in one book, then he/she can refer another book at the same time.</p>\r\n\r\n<hr />\r\n<p><strong>12. Can more than one student work on the same book?</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p>No, a particular textbook companion should be completed by only one student.</p>\r\n\r\n<hr />\r\n<p><strong>13. How many books can I propose?</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p>Initially, an applicant can propose 3 books. One of the proposed books will then be allotted for creating TBC. However, if a student is currently working on a particular book, then no other book should be proposed until the previously allotted book has been completed successfully.</p>\r\n\r\n<hr />\r\n<p><strong>14. Can I mail and ask if a book can be submitted for the book proposal?</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p>Before you mail us *please check the Completed Books and Books Under Progress section* to get an idea as to whether the book can be suggested.</p>\r\n\r\n<hr />\r\n<p><strong>15. Can I mail my book proposal?</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p>No. Please use the book proposal form to submit your proposal.</p>\r\n\r\n<hr />\r\n<p><strong>16. Can I propose a book that has been completed or is under progress as a different edition?</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p>No. Please ensure that the book chosen by you is not being worked upon/completed by any other student.</p>\r\n\r\n<hr />\r\n<p><strong>17. Do I need to know OpenFOAM before I submit my book proposal?</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p>The student should be comfortable with using OpenFOAM and should be aware of basic OpenFOAM commands and operations.</p>\r\n\r\n<hr />\r\n<p><strong>18. Can I refer to some cases as reference?</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p>Yes, the solved cases for completed books under TBC activity are available for free downloading. The cases can be referred if needed.</p>\r\n\r\n<hr />\r\n<p><strong>19. Can I use some other computing package for creating TBC?</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p>No proprietary packages should be used for creating TBC. For use of any free/libre and open source software package other than OpenFOAM, contact us at cfd (underscore) tbc (at) fossee (dot) in.</p>\r\n\r\n<hr />\r\n<h4><strong>20. When can I start the solving the cases?</strong></h4>\r\n\r\n<p>You can start solving as soon as the book proposed by you is approved and book allotment is confirmed. The confirmation will be communicated via an automated e-mail.</p>\r\n\r\n<hr />\r\n<p><strong>21. I have completed the solved examples for the entire textbook. What do I do now?</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p>Please contact the OpenFOAM team at cfd-tbc (at) fossee (dot) in and let them know that your examples from book are complete.</p>\r\n\r\n<hr />\r\n<p><strong>22. When do I submit the internship forms?</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p>You can submit the forms at any time after your book proposal has been accepted. Please note that your honorarium will not be released until all the correctly filled forms are received by CFD Team at IIT Bombay.</p>\r\n\r\n<hr />\r\n<p><strong>23. Is there a deadline for submitting the internship forms?</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p>No, there is no definite deadline for submitting the forms. However, the honorarium cannot be released unless the forms are received. Also, the book will not be published on the CFD website before receiving all the correctly filled forms.</p>\r\n\r\n<hr />\r\n<p><strong>24. What about intellectual rights of the TBC?</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p>The copyrights for TBC will be handed to FOSSEE Project. The name of creator of TBC and teacher will be published along with the pdf file. The TBC will be available for free downloading on CFD website.</p>\r\n\r\n<hr />\r\n<p><strong>25. What is the procedure for acquiring certificates/honorarium?</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p>The uploaded examples will be reviewed and once the cases are found satisfactory the applicant will be informed. The candidate should then mail ALL the internship related forms AFTER filling the appropriate details to IIT Bombay to the following address: Prof. Shivasubramanian Gopalakrishnan, Department of Mechanical Engineering, IIT Bombay, Powai, Mumbai 400 076 Ph: 022 2576 4133 Please write \"Textbook Companion\" on top of the envelope. The honorarium will then be sent via post after all the duly filled forms are received by OpenFOAM Team at IIT Bombay. The e-certificate can be downloaded from http://cfd.fossee.in/certificate after the solved examples are approved. You need to login in order to download the e-certificate. Please send ALL the correctly filled forms in a SINGLE envelope.</p>\r\n\r\n<hr />\r\n<p><strong>26. How long does it take to receive my Honorarium?</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p>If you do not get your money within 45 days after submitting cases, please get in touch with us - we shall be happy to assist you. If there are problems with the submitted cases, naturally, there will be further delays.</p>\r\n\r\n<hr />\r\n<p><strong>27. Why is there a delay in my Honorarium payment?</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p>On submission of a Textbook Companion, the review process involves several checks including but not limited to: 1. Incorrect Case file. 2. Completeness of the book - missing parts (or) sections of case files. In this regards, we are forced to test EVERY example of EVERY participant thoroughly. Due to many participants, this verification process takes considerable amount of time. Moreover, dispatch of Government money requires approvals from the Dean\'s Office, Accounts Office, Post Office, etc which also takes some time. Due to the above listed reasons, immediate acceptance of a Textbook Companion and processing of payment is highly impossible.</p>\r\n\r\n<hr />\r\n<p><strong>28. Where do I get a one-rupee revenue stamp? How does a revenue stamp look like?</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p>You can buy a one rupee revenue stamp from the Post Office. Here is a scan of a fully filled internship form - http://cfd.fossee.in/files/download/forms/example-filled-receipt.pdf</p>\r\n\r\n<hr />\r\n<p><strong>29. Can I propose more books after completion?</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p>Yes. You are welcome to propose more books. Please encourage your friends to take part in this internship.</p>\r\n\r\n<hr />\r\n<p><strong>30. I have finished one or more textbook companions already. Is there any other activity I can participate in?</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p>You can take part in <a href=\"http://cfd.fossee.in/lab-migration-project\">CFD Lab Migration Project</a> and <a href=\"http://python.fossee.in/textbook-companion-project/\">Python Textbook Companion Project.</a></p>\r\n\r\n<hr />\r\n<p><strong>31. Who do I contact in case I still have a doubt?</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p>You can contact the OpenFOAM team at cfd-tbc (at) fossee (dot) in.</p>\r\n\r\n<hr />',	'',	'full_html'),
('page',	0,	29,	29,	'und',	0,	'<p><strong>Forms related to Textbook Companion Internship </strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p>You may download following forms related to Textbook Companion Internship. These forms are to be filled and should be sent to the address given at the bottom of this page.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong><u>Please send ALL the forms in a SINGLE envelope. &#39;Forms&#39; not sent together shall not be considered in any circumstances. </u> </strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ol>\r\n	<li><a href=\"http://cfd.fossee.in/sites/default/files/OpenFOAM_InternshipForm.pdf\" target=\"_blank\">Internship Form</a></li>\r\n	<li><a href=\"http://cfd.fossee.in/sites/default/files/OpenFOAM-CopyRightTransferForm.pdf\" target=\"_blank\">Copyright Transfer Form</a></li>\r\n	<li><a href=\"http://cfd.fossee.in/sites/default/files/OpenFOAM-UnderTakingForm.pdf\" target=\"_blank\">Undertaking Form </a>(only if u have a mentor)</li>\r\n	<li><a href=\"http://cfd.fossee.in/sites/default/files/OpenFOAM-ReceiptForm.pdf\" target=\"_blank\">Receipt Form</a></li>\r\n   <!-- <li><a href=\"http://scilab.in/files/download/forms/Guidelines.pdf\">Guidelines</a></br >\r\n    </li> \r\n    <li><a href=\"http://scilab.in/files/download/forms/example-filled-receipt.pdf\">Example-Filled-Receipt</a><br />\r\n    </li>-->\r\n</ol>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p>The <strong>mailing address</strong> for these forms is</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Prof. Shivasubramanian Gopalakrishnan, </strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Dept. of Mechanical Engineering, </strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; IIT Bombay, Powai, Mumbai&nbsp; 400 076</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p><br />\r\nPlease write &quot;<strong>OpenFOAM Textbook Companion</strong>&quot; on top of the envelope.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\nFor the queries related to submission of forms please contact <a href=\"mailto:cfd-tbc@fossee.in\" target=\"_blank\">cfd-tbc(at)fossee(dot)in</a>.\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>',	'',	'full_html'),
('page',	0,	30,	30,	'und',	0,	'<hr />\r\n<p><a href=\"https://spoken-tutorial.org/tutorial-search/?search_foss=OpenFOAM+version+7&amp;search_language=\">Click here</a>&nbsp;to access the OpenFOAM Spoken Tutorials.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>The <a href=\"https://spoken-tutorial.org/about-us/\">Spoken Tutorial project</a> is about teaching and learning a particular Free/Libre and Open Source Software via an easy video tool. It is a screencast of approximately 10 mintutes with running commentary, a recording of computer session created for self learning.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>FOSSEE CFD team has created a series of Spoken Tutorials on OpenFOAM 7 which contains tutorials on solving cases using different OpenFOAM solvers.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Prerequisites for OpenFOAM Spoken Tutorials:</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ol>\r\n	<li>User should have basic knowledge of Computational Fluid Dynamics (CFD). You can view courses on CFD on NPTEL website <a href=\"https://nptel.ac.in/courses/112/105/112105254/\">here</a>.</li>\r\n	<li>User should have basic knowledge of Linux Terminal Commands, as OpenFOAM is accessed through terminal. <a href=\"https://cfd.direct/openfoam/linux-guide/\">Click here</a> to go through basic Linux Commands for OpenFOAM. You can also go through Linux Spoken Tutorials <a href=\"https://spoken-tutorial.org/tutorial-search/?search_foss=Linux&amp;search_language=English\">here</a>.</li>\r\n</ol>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>To install OpenFOAM 7</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p>For Ubuntu Linux Operating Systems 16.04 onwards the <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1tyfGDvG9huxhr0yUAXaP1WN0lnElo9TL/view?usp=sharing\">Installation manual</a> is available.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>While watching the Spoken Tutorials, you need to refer to the <a href=\"https://spoken-tutorial.org/media/videos/141/OpenFOAM-version-7-Instruction-Sheet-English.pdf\">Instruction Sheet</a> in parallel.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><a href=\"https://spoken-tutorial.org/tutorial-search/?search_foss=OpenFOAM+version+7&amp;search_language=\">Click here</a> to access the OpenFOAM Spoken Tutorials.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Spoken Tutorials on OpenFOAM</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p>Using these Spoken Tutorials, one can conduct SELF (Spoken Tutorial based Education and Learning through Free FLOSS study) workshops. <a href=\"http://process.spoken-tutorial.org/index.php/Software-Training#About_SELF_Workshops\" target=\"_blank\">Click here</a> to know more about SELF workshops, salient features and benefits.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>The Spoken Tutorial project is an initiative of the \"Talk to a Teacher\" project under the National Mission on Education through Information and Communication Technology, launched by MHRD, Govt of India.</p>\r\n',	'',	'full_html'),
('page',	0,	31,	31,	'und',	0,	'<div>\r\n<div><strong>OpenFOAM Weblinks</strong>:\r\n<div>\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li><a href=\"https://cfd.direct/openfoam/user-guide/\" target=\"_blank\">OpenFOAM Documentation</a></li>\r\n	<li><a href=\"https://cpp.openfoam.org/v4/\" target=\"_blank\">OpenFOAM C++ source guide</a></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n<div>\r\n<div><strong>OpenFOAM Wikipedia</strong>:\r\n\r\n<div>\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li><a href=\"http://openfoamwiki.net/index.php/Main_Page\" target=\"_blank\">OpenFOAM Wikipage</a></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<div>\r\n<div><strong>OpenFOAM Extended Project</strong>:\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li><a href=\"http://www.extend-project.de/\" target=\"_blank\">OpenFOAM Extended Project</a></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<div>\r\n<div><!--<strong>OpenFOAM Workshop 2014</strong></span>:</div><div><ul><li><a href=\"http://www.icnaam.org/nafluids/Workshop-on-OpenFOAM\" target=\"_blank\">ICNAAM</a></li><li><a href=\"http://serve.me.nus.edu.sg/shuchang/OpenFOAM2014.htm\" target=\"_blank\">NUS Singapore</a></li></ul></div></div><p>&nbsp;</p>--></div>\r\n</div>\r\n',	'',	'full_html'),
('page',	0,	32,	32,	'und',	0,	'<center>\r\n  <a href=\"http://scilab.in\" target=\"_blank\">\r\n    <img src=\"http://fossee.in/sites/all/themes/fossee/img/scilab-logo.png\" />\r\n  </a>\r\n</center>\r\n<p style=\"text-align:justify;\">\r\n  Scilab software, stemming from Inria, France is the worldwide open source reference in numerical computation software. Please see www.scilab.org for more details. Scilab is used in all major strategic scientific areas of industry and services such as space, aeronautics, automotive, energy, defense, finance and transport.\r\n</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align:justify;\">\r\n  We, the Scilab team at IIT Bombay India, aim to increase the use of Scilab in educational institutions across India. The primary focus of our efforts is to help educational institutions shift from using proprietary packages to using Scilab. Scilab is a major component of the FOSSEE (Free and Open source Software for Education) project. The goal of this project is to enable the students and faculty of various colleges/institutes/universities across India to use Open Source Software tools for all their computational needs, thereby improving the quality of instruction, learning and to avoid expensive licences of computational tools for research and education.\r\n</p>\r\n<center>\r\n    <b>Visit:</b> <a href=\"http://scilab.in\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"text-decoration:none;\"> http://scilab.in </a>\r\n</center>',	'',	'full_html'),
('page',	0,	34,	34,	'und',	0,	'<p>The CFD Textbook Companion project is managed by the FOSSEE project, IIT Bombay. Textbook Companion internship is a programme for college students who are willing to undertake an internship with FOSSEE, IIT Bombay. The project will require a teacher as a mentor. The mentor must have taught the specific subject for at least one year. The mentor will guide the student through the project and will be responsible for the student/intern\'s submissions.</p>\r\n\r\n<h4>The procedure is as follows:</h4>\r\n\r\n<ol>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p>You are required to learn OpenFOAM. Resources are provided at <a href=\"http://spoken-tutorial.org/tutorial-search/?search_foss=OpenFOAM&amp;search_language=English\" target=\"_blank\">OpenFOAM Resources</a>. Learning OpenFOAM is easy and if someone listens to and practices the Spoken Tutorials on OpenFOAM, it can be learned in 7-8 days. For use of any software package other than OpenFOAM, contact us at <a href=\"mailto:contact-cfd@fossee.in\" target=\"_blank\">contact-cfd (at) fossee(dot)in</a></p>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p>You could propose three books in the order of your preference, using the proposal form available <a href=\"textbook-companion/proposal\">here</a>. You have to create a new account and log in to access the proposal form. You must ensure that the books you are proposing have not been been completed or undertaken under this project. Click on <a href=\"textbook-companion/completed-books\">Completed Books</a> and <a href=\"textbook-companion/books-in-progress\">Books in Progress</a> to see the respective lists.</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p>Please make sure that the book proposed by you has at least 20 examples. If it is found that the number of examples is less, the internship might be canceled during the later stages. Along with the book proposal, you are required to send a typical chapter\'s case file from one of the three proposed books to <a href=\"mailto:cfd-tbc@fossee.in\" target=\"_blank\">cfd-tbc (at) fossee (dot) in</a> in a .zip or .tgz file. We will not contact you to send the cases. It is suggested that you propose the book as early as possible since your preferred book may be assigned to someone else.</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p><strong>It has been found that a few students are putting their friends\' name as mentor. In order to prevent this, the mentor details will be verified.</strong></p>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>Please send us either of the following as proof for mentor ID verification:\r\n	<ol>\r\n		<li>Link to the official faculty web-page (to be sent to <a href=\"mailto:cfd-tbc@fossee.in\" target=\"_blank\">cfd-tbc (at) fossee (dot) in</a>)</li>\r\n		<li>Copy of letter from head of the department on institute/college letterhead&nbsp;stating that particular person is staff member of the mentioned department. The student should send the scanned copy of the letter before the book proposal is approved. The hard-copy of the letter should be sent along with the internship forms.</li>\r\n	</ol>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li><strong>Please note that the book proposal will not be approved if required proof of identification is not submitted. </strong>\r\n	<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p>We will try to allot one of the three proposed books to you. You will be intimated about the approval or rejection of your proposal via e-mail within 3 days. Your name along with the proposed textbook will appear under <a href=\"textbook-companion/books-in-progress\">Books in Progress</a>.</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p>After the final allotment, you will start solving only the solved examples of the entire book. You are required to upload the solved cases on the interface. Also, send the code to your mentor.</p>\r\n\r\n	<p>Note: Lack of regularity on your part may force us to cancel your internship and the book will be assigned to another intern. Simultaneously, you should fill the IITB registration form and post it to us. All the required forms are available at <a href=\"textbook-companion/internship-forms\">Required Internship Forms</a></p>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p>The time-frame for completion of solved examples will be decided together by you, your mentor and us.</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p><strong>Review of the book -</strong> The review of the book will typically take approximately <strong>20 working days</strong> to finish. If any example is found to be not producing the desired result during review process, the student will have to recheck and resubmit all the examples. Each time you submit the examples, it will be queued up with other review requests and will result in subsequent delays and <a href=\"textbook-companion/tbc-honorarium\" target=\"_blank\">revision </a> of your honorarium.</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p>Candidates who successfully finish the textbook companion as per the specified procedure will be awarded an internship e-certificate: \"Certified that the work completed is equivalent to six weeks of training under the supervision of the concerned faculty of IIT Bombay\".</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p>You will be awarded an honorarium of ₹ 10,000 and your mentor ₹ 5,000 for completing this work. For details please <a href=\"textbook-companion/tbc-honorarium\">click here</a>.</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n</ol>\r\n\r\n<p>For any further queries&nbsp;or clarifications, please contact us at the following email address:<br />\r\n<a href=\"mailto:cfd-tbc@fossee.in\" target=\"_blank\">cfd-tbc (at) fossee (dot) in</a>.</p>\r\n',	'',	'full_html'),
