INSERT INTO `node_revision__field_source` (`bundle`, `deleted`, `entity_id`, `revision_id`, `langcode`, `delta`, `field_source_value`, `field_source_summary`, `field_source_format`) VALUES
('credentials',	0,	19,	19,	'und',	0,	'<p>Easily accessible. Easy to learn, since it\'s very well documented and has a lot of discussion forums. Also, the availability of source files, makes it easier to actually realize and appreciate its working and gives sense of control over it and helps in understanding the underlying computations and physics, rather than working on a \"black box\" which is the case with most of other tools of comparable capability.</p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"rteright\">- Gaurav Chaudhary, Student, IIT Bombay</p>\r\n',	'',	'full_html'),
('credentials',	0,	20,	20,	'und',	0,	'<p>I Started using OpenFOAM last semester in Feb, 2013. In the start, it took a while to get used to all the file system but later it became normal.Customization of problem\'s physics is very easy unlike other packages whereediting is restricted after a level.</p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"rteright\">- Shambhu Yadav, M.Tech, Propulsion, Department Of Aerospace Engineering, Indian Institute of Technology, Bombay</p>\r\n',	'',	'full_html'),
('credentials',	0,	21,	21,	'und',	0,	'<p>I had never been introduced to OpenFOAM until last semester. So initially it took me some time to understand how to go about it, but once I got a hang of it, I could work well with it. The video tutorials were of great help.</p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"rteright\">- Priyanka Patki, M.Tech ,Thermal and Fluids Dept of Mechanical Engineering IIT Bombay</p>\r\n',	'',	'full_html'),
('credentials',	0,	22,	22,	'und',	0,	'<p>I used OpenFOAM for my class assignment for \"Turbulence and Combustion\" in Spring 2012 at IITB, in which I asked the students to solve for turbulent channel flow at high Reynolds number using RANS (Reynolds Averaged Navier Stokes) models and compare the output with Direct Numerical Simulation data. I referred students to the FOSSEE spoken tutorial website for learning the basics of OpenFOAM, which they found to be very useful. One of the big advantages of using OpenFOAM was that the students could simply download the software into their laptops for free, and I did not have to worry about giving them access to any licenses. Moreover, the students were able to learn the software fairly quickly, and got a great hands-on learning experience on using RANS models.</p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"rteright\">- Amitabh Bhattacharya, Assistant Professor, Mechanical Engineering, IIT Bombay, Powai, Mumbai</p>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n',	'',	'full_html'),
('credentials',	0,	241,	241,	'und',	0,	'<p>My M.Tech supervisor asked me to learn OpenFOAM. At that moment, I didn\'t have any idea about this FOSS.&nbsp;I started with YouTube videos and found Spoken Tutorials of FOSSEE, IITB. They explained the basics of OpenFOAM very well. The Spoken Tutorials helped me a lot in the learning of this FOSS. Later, I got the opportunity to come to IITB for the FOSSEE fellowship program. I met the professors, mentors and the other fellows there. &nbsp;They helped me to solve some problems on which I was facing difficulty earlier. So, my experience with FOSSEE was very good.&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"rteright\">- Jishnu Handique, Research Assistant, NIT Manipur</p>\r\n',	'',	'full_html'),
('credentials',	0,	242,	242,	'und',	0,	'<p>FOSSEE IIT Bombay provided me great opportunity to understand what CFD and OpenFOAM really is. I had the opportunity to apply OpenFOAM over INS Vikramaditya model and studied the multiphase pressure and velocity characteristics in the domain. The mentors Mr. Sathish and Ms. Deepa were very supportive. It was an overall fulfilling experience, and anyone looking for exposure should definitely apply.</p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"rteright\">- <span class=\"qu\" role=\"gridcell\" tabindex=\"-1\"><span class=\"gD\" data-hovercard-id=\"siddhantsaraswat.16me271@nitk.edu.in\" data-hovercard-owner-id=\"132\" name=\"Siddhant Saraswat\">Siddhant Saraswat, </span></span>Student, NITK surathkal</p>\r\n\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">&nbsp;</div>\r\n',	'',	'full_html'),
('credentials',	0,	243,	243,	'und',	0,	'<p>OpenFOAM and FOSSEE are the key to access such an complex Engineering material. When I started using OpenFOAM, every commercial&nbsp;software seems easy and less detail oriented. OpenFOAM gives wide access to compile and modify problem, solver and data. Best part are Video tutorial and open access to reports and case study on FOSSEE website. After learning, anybody can contribute to develop software and to improve documentation by making real engineering problem case studies.</p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"rteright\">- Divyesh Variya, Student, Government Engineering College, Valsad, Gujarat</p>\r\n',	'',	'full_html'),
('credentials',	0,	244,	244,	'und',	0,	'<p>It is usually argued that OpenFOAM has a very steep learning curve. But with the IIT Bombay Spoken Tutorials, this learning curve can be tackled with relative ease. Unlike other commercial software, OpenFOAM is easily accessible, free of charge and setting up OpenFOAM is very easy. The availability of source code helped my dive deep into the numerical schemes used in any problem I was trying to solve. OpenFOAM comes with enough tutorials that help beginners who have difficulty setting up cases from the scratch.</p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"rteright\">- Ashley Melvin, Student, IIT Bombay</p>\r\n',	'',	'full_html'),
('credentials',	0,	245,	245,	'und',	0,	'<p>The first time I started using OpenFOAM is not very back in the past. Before, I used to use ANSYS for my needs. It was hard to start learning OpenFOAM in the beginning. I slowly made progress by watching YouTube, spoken tutorials and some other documents available online. But once you learn OpenFOAM, you usually don\'t like anything else. It is more detailed and conceptual than any other CFD software. If anyone is hoping to skyrocket their carrier in CFD, then OpenFOAM is the best choice. We ordinarily do not find people working on OpenFOAM, especially in India. It is the FOSSEE that has taken a step forward to spread the name of this FOSS among the young minds of India. FOSSEE conducts a summer internship every year where talents from all over India come together and work together. The best thing about this internship is that candidates are chosen based on their capabilities, not GPA or college. There is a perfect working environment for excelling one\'s knowledge and experience. Give this internship a try if you love CFD. Keep FOAMing.</p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"rteright\">- Raj Niraj Patil, Student, NIT Agartala</p>\r\n',	'',	'full_html'),
('credentials',	0,	246,	246,	'und',	0,	'<p>OpenFOAM is really a powerful tool to analyze complex problems in a really straightforward way. It took a bit of time to grasp the basics, but once that&nbsp;is done, one can further play along with it with any possible given situation.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>FOSSEE and IIT Bombay is a good place to work, Dr. Shivasubramanian had really good problems for OpenFOAM and Sathish and Deepa were really supportive and guided us well through the process. I would recommend any beginner in CFD to use OpenFOAM. I appreciate FOSSEE\'s work in getting people to use OpenFOAM and other open source softwares.</p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"rteright\">- Vishish Behera, Student, SRM University Chennai</p>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n',	'',	'full_html'),
('credentials',	0,	247,	247,	'und',	0,	'<p>My hands on openfoam</p>\r\n\r\n<p>OpenFOAM is a unique tool to understand CFD and has been a perfect book to understand the foundational aspects of computational sciences. Unlike conventional methods that restricts us from venturing into the skeleton of the software, OpenFOAM gives us the advantage of exploring and manipulating the techniques involved as it is a openware and is efficient enough for innovations to be incorporated.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Fossee at IIT Bombay has been a good support in connecting many students to easy access and learning of computer thereby bridging&nbsp;the gap in computer litreracy in steps.The Fossee CFD module being OpenFOAM, have made a better link to computer literacy computational skills and underlying physics,thus completing the education picture.</p>\r\n\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">My fellowship at FOSSEE had me exposed to the ways in which, developers can explore the soffware and students can change the education scenario through FOSS and Outreach.</div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"rteright\" dir=\"auto\">- Bhaskar Srinivasan, Student, Centre for Space Science Technology Education in Asia Pacific</div>\r\n',	'',	'full_html'),
('credentials',	0,	248,	248,	'und',	0,	'<p>I’ve been using OpenFOAM for my final year project and I gained some experience through my project, but I lacked a community which supports and helps to learn OpenFOAM. FOSSEE gave what I was lacking, it provided a platform for learning and sharing knowledge. I got to meet lots of people who are interested in OpenFOAM from different parts of India. A great thanks to Mr. Sathish and Ms. Deepa for being our mentor and Dr. Shivasubramanian Gopalakrishnan for guiding us through the fellowship.</p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"rteright\">- Vignesh S.P, Student, Sri Ramakrishna Engineering College, Coimbatore</p>\r\n',	'',	'full_html'),
('credentials',	0,	257,	257,	'und',	0,	'<div dir=\"auto\" style=\"color: rgb(80, 0, 80); font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small;\">\r\n<p>From FOSSEE Summer Fellowship to an internship</p>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p>My journey with OpenFOAM started with the Spoken Tutorial programme by the FOSSEE team. Due to the nature of OpenSource software documentation and tutorials, sometimes finding the right tutorials that explain the basics is very difficult but with the help of Spoken Tutorials I was able to easily grasp the workings of OpenFOAM and learn my way upto to more complex problems.This also helped me during the task phase for the FOSSEE Fellowship 2020, as I&nbsp;developed a good understanding of the basics in OpenFOAM, I&nbsp;was successfully able to complete the screening task phase and get selected for the Fellowship.&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p>During the fellowship, Professor Janani Srree, Swetha and the rest of the FOSSEE team were incredible in their support and guidance. Even though in 2020 we were faced with lockdowns, the fellowship was conducted through online modes and this did not take away from the fantastic experience and the knowledge that was gained while doing the projects.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p>I would also like to thank my mentors Ashley Melvin &amp; Divyesh Variya for their&nbsp;constant support.&nbsp;Professor Janani had some very interesting projects for us related to COVID-19 specific research that could be performed using OpenFOAM, specifically in multiphase solvers such as twoPhaseEulerFoam. Later, I also got the opportunity to test my knowledge that I gained in OpenFOAM by acting as a Teaching Assistant (TA) in one of the workshops conducted by FOSSEE.&nbsp;A company called UFI filters had approached Prof. Janani for an intern to work&nbsp; in OpenFOAM and I was recommended by her! I am currently working with them to solve complex flow problems using OpenFOAM. So overall the FOSSEE Fellowship&nbsp; has led to a very successful and fulfilling outcome!!</p>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Regards&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Sahil Deepak Kukian</p>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n</div>\r\n',	'',	'full_html'),
('credentials',	0,	267,	267,	'und',	0,	'<p><a href=\"https://static.fossee.in/cfd/videos/testimonial-ashuthosh.mp4\">Video Testimonial by Mr. Ashutosh PS</a>.&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n',	'',	'full_html'),
('credentials',	0,	268,	268,	'und',	0,	'<p><a href=\"https://static.fossee.in/cfd/videos/testimonial-divyesh.mp4\">Video Testimonial by Mr. Divyesh Variya</a></p>\r\n',	'',	'full_html'),
('credentials',	0,	270,	270,	'und',	0,	'<p><a href=\"https://static.fossee.in/cfd/videos/testimonial-ashley.mp4\">Video testimonial by Mr. Ashley Melvin</a></p>\r\n',	'',	'full_html'),
('credentials',	0,	271,	271,	'und',	0,	'<p><a href=\"https://static.fossee.in/cfd/videos/testimonial-mano.mp4\">Video testimonial by Mr. Mano Prithviraj</a></p>\r\n',	'',	'full_html'),
('credentials',	0,	275,	275,	'und',	0,	'<p>Mr. Tinto Thomas was an intern in the FOSSEE Summer Fellowship 2022 under the OpenFOAM Project. Please <a href=\"https://www.linkedin.com/in/tintothomas59/recent-activity/\">click here </a>to view his testimonial in LinkedIn</p>\r\n',	'',	'full_html'),
('credentials',	0,	297,	297,	'und',	0,	'<p><strong>Testimonial by Mr. Chaitanya Apte</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"color: rgb(34, 34, 34); font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small;\">\"FOSSEE Summer Fellowship 2022 was the first&nbsp;time I used an open source software. After&nbsp;working on OpenFOAM I got&nbsp;to&nbsp;know what actually goes on behind the scenes in a CFD simulation unlike the commercial packages. Additionally, I learnt a lot from the projects other interns were working on. My mentor Mano Prithiviraj and guide Prof. Naren were quite helpful throughout the internship. I developed a holistic understanding of CAE which helped me further in my career. I think this fellowship is a good starting&nbsp;point for anyone interested in numerical simulations.\"</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"color: rgb(34, 34, 34); font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small;\">Chaitanya Apte, VJTI, Mumbai, Maharashtra</span></p>\r\n',	'',	'full_html'),
('credentials',	0,	298,	298,	'und',	0,	'<p>Mohammed Saqlain expresses his gratitude towards the OpenFOAM team, FOSSEE. Please find his testimonial in the following link:<br />\r\n<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1lDDhgJS4cLxCLD3nc0j-JKQth_5NETZbp2b-gIjOl44/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1lDDhgJS4cLxCLD3nc0j-JKQth_5NETZbp2b-gIjOl44/edit?usp=sharing</a></p>\r\n',	'',	'full_html'),
('credentials',	0,	335,	335,	'und',	0,	'<p><strong>Testimonial by Mr. Rajdeep Adak</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"color: rgb(34, 34, 34); font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small;\">I joined FOSSEE in 2021 as an intern. I was deeply inspired by FOSSEE\'s vision to develop free and open-source equivalents to industrial scientific software. FOSSEE is managed by the renowned faculty of IIT Bombay, who make this endeavor possible. At FOSSEE, I worked with Prof. J. S. Murallidharan and Prof. Prabhu Ramachandran, and developed software for fluid dynamics simulation. The exposure to fluid mechanics helped me discover an interest in the broader field of Dynamical Systems. Today, I’m proud to be starting a PhD at Arizona State University in the same field, tackling complex control problems in high-precision polymer manufacturing. FOSSEE has been instrumental in enabling me to reach the doorstep of a PhD. My research journey started at FOSSEE, and I still continue to assist the CFD-FOSSEE team. FOSSEE offers an excellent environment for students to explore research and take ownership of their work - which I believe is paramount towards building a successful career in both industry and academia.</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"color: rgb(34, 34, 34); font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small;\">-&nbsp;</span>Mr. Rajdeep Adak, PhD student at The Arizona State University (Former Reserach Associate at FOSSEE, IIT Bombay)</p>\r\n',	'',	'full_html'),
('credentials',	0,	337,	337,	'und',	0,	'<p><strong>Testimonial by Mr. Biraj Khadka</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p>FOSSEE has been instrumental in shaping my path as a researcher. I started as a summer intern, where I performed a CFD simulation of single-phase flow in a stirred tank reactor using OpenFOAM, under the guidance of Prof. Raghvendra Gupta. Later, as a Research Assistant, I collaborated with Prof. Janani Srree Murallidharan and the FOSSEE team to develop OpenFOAM tutorials and mentor interns. I am currently a PhD student specializing in BioFluid Dynamics and often rely on the core concepts and practical skills I gained through FOSSEE.&nbsp; The combination of high-quality resources, expert guidance, and a collaborative environment makes it an exceptional learning platform. I recommend FOSSEE to anyone looking to build or strengthen their expertise in Computational Fluid Dynamics.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><br />\r\nBiraj Khadka<br />\r\nPhD student,<br />\r\nUniversity of Rochester</p>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n',	'',	'full_html'),
('credentials',	0,	346,	346,	'und',	0,	'<p><span style=\"color:#2980b9;\"><strong>Testimonial by Mr. Jinu Chandran (FOSSEE Summer Fellow, OpenFOAM category, 2025)- BITS Goa</strong></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>FOSSEE OpenFOAM Summer Fellowship 2025 - Internship Experience</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<div><br />\r\nI am deeply grateful to FOSSEE for selecting me for the Summer Fellowship Program 2025, which has been an enriching experience that significantly enhanced my understanding of computational fluid dynamics through OpenFOAM. The fellowship was exceptionally well-organised with weekly meetings, as these regular sessions with the supervising professor allowed us to discuss progress, address challenges, and plan upcoming work effectively, ensuring I could complete my internship objectives within the stipulated timeframe. One of the program\'s greatest strengths was the mentor assignment system, where having a dedicated mentor was invaluable, particularly during the initial phases when navigating OpenFOAM\'s complex interface and functionalities felt overwhelming. Learning that my internship work will be featured as a case study project on the FOSSEE platform is incredibly motivating, as this recognition not only validates the effort I invested but also serves as a strong incentive to continue my exploration of OpenFOAM and computational fluid dynamics, knowing that my work might help future learners navigate similar challenges and adds meaningful purpose to the entire experience.</div>\r\n\r\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\r\n\r\n<div>\r\n<p>Again, thank you for this incredible opportunity and the excellent support throughout the program.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Best regards,<br />\r\nJinu Chandran</p>\r\n</div>\r\n',	'',	'full_html'),
('credentials',	0,	349,	349,	'und',	0,	'<p><span style=\"color:#2980b9;\"><strong>Testimonial by Mr. Shreyas Shrestha (FOSSEE Summer Fellow, OpenFOAM category, 2025)- Tribhuvan University</strong></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>FOSSEE OpenFOAM Summer Fellowship 2025 - Experience</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p>What started as a one-day workshop on the basics of OpenFOAM turned into an incredible journey through the FOSSEE Summer Fellowship 2025. After completing the screening activities, I had the opportunity to work with supportive mentors who guided me throughout the project. During my fellowship, I worked on a research migration project that involved simulating non-Newtonian flows in OpenFOAM. This experience helped me develop practical skills in simulation, from case setup and analysis to conducting research and writing papers. Beyond technical knowledge, it taught me patience and the value of collaboration. I am very grateful to the FOSSEE team and my mentors for making this journey both memorable and impactful.</p>\r\n',	'',	'full_html'),
('credentials',	0,	351,	351,	'und',	0,	'<p><span style=\"color:#2980b9;\"><strong>Testimonial by Mr. Barani Ilango Balan</strong><strong>, FOSSEE Summer Fellow from Manipal Institute of Technology</strong></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p>I am sincerely grateful to FOSSEE for giving me the opportunity to be part of the Summer Fellowship Program 2025. The experience has been truly transformative, deepening my knowledge of computational fluid dynamics and enhancing my skills in OpenFOAM.&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p>The fellowship was very well structured, with weekly review meetings that helped me stay on track and receive valuable feedback from my supervisor. These sessions provided the perfect platform to discuss challenges, refine approaches, and maintain consistent progress throughout the project. The guidance and mentorship I received were instrumental in helping me tackle complex simulation problems and improve both my technical and analytical understanding of CFD workflows.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>One of the most rewarding moments was learning that my project will be featured as a case study on the FOSSEE platform. Knowing that my work could assist future learners in understanding OpenFOAM and its applications is both motivating and fulfilling.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>I truly appreciate the entire FOSSEE team for their constant support and encouragement throughout the fellowship. This experience has been a major step forward in my journey as a CFD enthusiast and has strengthened my resolve to continue exploring advanced simulation research.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Best Regards<br />\r\nBarani Ilango Balan</p>\r\n',	'',	'full_html');
