(240,	'und',	'node_search',	' fossee summer fellowship 2019 fossee summer fellowship 2019 fossee cfd team iit bombay invites applications for summer fellowship 2019 selected candidates will get an opportunity to do an internship in iit bombay  on free libre and open source cfd simulation under prof janani srree murallidharan from mechanical engineering department registration  the registration for fossee summer fellowship 2019 starts on 1 february 2019 for registration click here  to view the complete list of projects click here   important dates  click here to know the important dates screening task  minimum 1 case study project  doing multiple case study projects will improve chances of fellowship  case study project involves solving a feasible cfd related problem statement of reasonable complexity in openfoam technical requirements   any student ug pg research scholars etc who has basic knowledge of computational fluid dynamics and openfoam  learn openfoam by visiting our spoken tutorials   procedure to submit   prepare a 1 page abstract describing the cfd problem statement make sure your proposal is not in the list under completed case studies and case studies in progress  to view a sample abstract click here once your proposal is submitted it will be reviewed and approved disapproved after receiving the approval of your proposal you can proceed to complete the case study project once you complete the project prepare a case study project directory in a zip format which has the following mesh file exported from cfd software like ansys gmsh salome or created using openfoam utilities simulated case directories using openfoam 404150 or foamextend 3140 contours plots and data files postprocessed using paraview and or python scripts minimum 3 page report of case study project in pdf format specifying software details and dependencies on other codes functions if any click here to view and download the completed case study project directory submit the proposal and case study project directory in the submission portal if not selected for fossee fellowship your project s will still be evaluated under cfd case study project after submission submission portal  1 you will receive an email with the subject line fossee summer fellowship 2019 submission 2 using the credentials provided click here to visit the submission portal 3 select cfd openfoam fsf 2019 under my courses section to submit the task s  note  to consider for fossee fellowship 2019 the case study proposals should only be submitted in the link using the username and password given in the registered email for fellowship program evaluation criteria   the completed case study project will be evaluated on complexity of the project validated results using other sources references quality of the report number of case studies submitted per candidate for any further queries contact us at  contactcfd at fossee dot in with subject line as  fossee fellowship 2019  cfdadmin mon 1282019 1110  ',	0),
(241,	'und',	'node_search',	' credentials by jishnu handique credentials by jishnu handique sathish thu 10032019 1042 my mtech supervisor asked me to learn openfoam at that moment i didn t have any idea about this foss i started with youtube videos and found spoken tutorials of fossee iitb they explained the basics of openfoam very well the spoken tutorials helped me a lot in the learning of this foss later i got the opportunity to come to iitb for the fossee fellowship program i met the professors mentors and the other fellows there they helped me to solve some problems on which i was facing difficulty earlier so my experience with fossee was very good jishnu handique research assistant nit manipur yes  ',	0),
(242,	'und',	'node_search',	' credentials by siddhant saraswat credentials by siddhant saraswat sathish thu 10032019 1109 fossee iit bombay provided me great opportunity to understand what cfd and openfoam really is i had the opportunity to apply openfoam over ins vikramaditya model and studied the multiphase pressure and velocity characteristics in the domain the mentors mr sathish and ms deepa were very supportive it was an overall fulfilling experience and anyone looking for exposure should definitely apply siddhant saraswat student nitk surathkal yes  ',	0),
(243,	'und',	'node_search',	' credentials by divyesh variya credentials by divyesh variya sathish thu 10032019 1112 openfoam and fossee are the key to access such an complex engineering material when i started using openfoam every commercial software seems easy and less detail oriented openfoam gives wide access to compile and modify problem solver and data best part are video tutorial and open access to reports and case study on fossee website after learning anybody can contribute to develop software and to improve documentation by making real engineering problem case studies divyesh variya student government engineering college valsad gujarat yes  ',	0),
(244,	'und',	'node_search',	' credentials by ashley melvin credentials by ashley melvin sathish thu 10032019 1117 it is usually argued that openfoam has a very steep learning curve but with the iit bombay spoken tutorials this learning curve can be tackled with relative ease unlike other commercial software openfoam is easily accessible free of charge and setting up openfoam is very easy the availability of source code helped my dive deep into the numerical schemes used in any problem i was trying to solve openfoam comes with enough tutorials that help beginners who have difficulty setting up cases from the scratch ashley melvin student iit bombay yes  ',	0),
(245,	'und',	'node_search',	' credentials by raj niraj patil credentials by raj niraj patil sathish fri 10042019 1419 the first time i started using openfoam is not very back in the past before i used to use ansys for my needs it was hard to start learning openfoam in the beginning i slowly made progress by watching youtube spoken tutorials and some other documents available online but once you learn openfoam you usually don t like anything else it is more detailed and conceptual than any other cfd software if anyone is hoping to skyrocket their carrier in cfd then openfoam is the best choice we ordinarily do not find people working on openfoam especially in india it is the fossee that has taken a step forward to spread the name of this foss among the young minds of india fossee conducts a summer internship every year where talents from all over india come together and work together the best thing about this internship is that candidates are chosen based on their capabilities not gpa or college there is a perfect working environment for excelling one s knowledge and experience give this internship a try if you love cfd keep foaming raj niraj patil student nit agartala yes  ',	0),
(246,	'und',	'node_search',	' credentials by vishish behera credentials by vishish behera sathish fri 10042019 1421 openfoam is really a powerful tool to analyze complex problems in a really straightforward way it took a bit of time to grasp the basics but once that is done one can further play along with it with any possible given situation fossee and iit bombay is a good place to work dr shivasubramanian had really good problems for openfoam and sathish and deepa were really supportive and guided us well through the process i would recommend any beginner in cfd to use openfoam i appreciate fossee s work in getting people to use openfoam and other open source softwares vishish behera student srm university chennai yes  ',	0),
(247,	'und',	'node_search',	' credentials by bhaskar srinivasan credentials by bhaskar srinivasan sathish fri 10042019 1424 my hands on openfoam openfoam is a unique tool to understand cfd and has been a perfect book to understand the foundational aspects of computational sciences unlike conventional methods that restricts us from venturing into the skeleton of the software openfoam gives us the advantage of exploring and manipulating the techniques involved as it is a openware and is efficient enough for innovations to be incorporated fossee at iit bombay has been a good support in connecting many students to easy access and learning of computer thereby bridging the gap in computer litreracy in stepsthe fossee cfd module being openfoam have made a better link to computer literacy computational skills and underlying physics thus completing the education picture my fellowship at fossee had me exposed to the ways in which developers can explore the soffware and students can change the education scenario through foss and outreach bhaskar srinivasan student centre for space science technology education in asia pacific yes  ',	0),
(248,	'und',	'node_search',	' credentials by vignesh sp credentials by vignesh sp sathish fri 10042019 1426 i ve been using openfoam for my final year project and i gained some experience through my project but i lacked a community which supports and helps to learn openfoam fossee gave what i was lacking it provided a platform for learning and sharing knowledge i got to meet lots of people who are interested in openfoam from different parts of india a great thanks to mr sathish and ms deepa for being our mentor and dr shivasubramanian gopalakrishnan for guiding us through the fellowship vignesh sp student sri ramakrishna engineering college coimbatore yes  ',	0),
(249,	'und',	'node_search',	' fossee summer fellowship 2020 fossee summer fellowship 2020 please keep visiting this page for updates last updated on 1 april 2020 due to the outbreak of covid19 and travel restrictions placed by iit bombay the fossee summer fellowship 2020 will be offered remotely the fossee team will contact the selected candidates through emails soon resources refer to  spoken tutorials on openfoam  to start learning openfoam screening task computational fluid dynamics cfd simulation using openfoam this task involves simulating a cfd problem in openfoam as well as the preparation of a technical report on the same submissions without the technical report will not be considered for evaluation a minimum of 2 case study project submissions are required to be considered for evaluation technical requirements  knowledge of computational fluid dynamics and openfoam procedure to submit  click here  to submit prepare a 1page abstract describing the cfd problem statement make sure your proposal is not in the list under completed case studies and case studies in progress  to view a sample abstract  click here  upload the prepared abstract using the abstract submission option in the fossee summer fellowship portal once your proposal is submitted it will be reviewed and approved disapproved after receiving the approval of your proposal you can proceed to complete the case study project once you complete the project prepare a case study project directory in a zip format which has the following mesh file exported from cfd software like ansys gmsh salome or created using openfoam utilities simulated case directories using openfoam 4041506070 or foamextend 314041 contours plots and data files postprocessed using paraview and or python scripts minimum 3page report of case study project in pdf format specifying software details and dependencies on other codes functions if any submit the case study project directory in the report and case file submission option in the fossee summer fellowship portal evaluation criteria  the completed case study project will be evaluated on the complexity of the project validation of results using other sources references quality of the report the number of case studies submitted per candidate multiple case study project submissions will improve the chances of landing the fellowship note  if not selected for fossee fellowship your project s will still be evaluated under  cfd case study project  after submission sashirekha wed 12112019 1303  ',	0),
(250,	'und',	'node_search',	' half day event on openfoam 2019 half day event on openfoam 2019 about the event cfd fossee team at iit bombay organized a halfday event on cfd and openfoam an open source toolbox used in academia and industry to solve continuum mechanics problems including computational fluid dynamics cfd this half day event was held at bannari amman institute of technology bit sathyamangalam on december 12 2019 and was attended by about 80 students from the sathyamangalam and coimbatore area prof janani srree murallidharan introduced the students to the basics of cfd and also mapped it to openfoam and its use as a continuum mechanics and computational fluid dynamics tool ms swetha manian sridhar spoke to the students about cfdfossee s case study activity wherein students can submit case studies and presented a case study which had been submitted by a student the case study activity helps a students improve their job potential and also fetches them an ecertificate and a handsome honorarium they also spoke about fossee s summer fellowship program for 2020 which they plan on rolling out shortly to qualify for this internship the students need to clear the screening task of a minimum of 2 two case study submission below is the event schedule  schedule date   12 december 2019  time   900 am 100 pm  venue   old mechanical engineering seminar hall bannari amman institute of technology sathyamanagalam tn  attendees   80 900 am 1030 am basics of computational fluid dynamics cfd prof janani srree murallidharan 1030 am 1045 am tea break 1045 am 1145 am basics of openfoam and its use as a continuum mechanics computational fluid dynamics tool prof janani srree murallidharan 1145 am 1200 pm about fossee and spoken tutorials ms swetha manian sridhar 1200 pm 1245 pm case study activity sample case study presentation f ossee summer fellowship 2020 ms swetha manian sridhar 1245 pm 100 pm open to questions and student interaction 100 pm break for lunch end of session  gallery sashirekha mon 1132020 1231  ',	0),
(251,	'und',	'node_search',	' half day event on openfoam at bannari amman dec 2019 half day event on openfoam at bannari amman dec 2019 halfday event on openfoam at bannari amman institute of technology bit sathyamangalam dec 2019 cfd fossee team at iit bombay organized a halfday event on cfd and openfoam an open source toolbox used in academia and industry to solve continuum mechanics problems including computational fluid dynamics cfd this half day event was held at bannari amman institute of technology bit sathyamangalam on december 12 2019 and was attended by about 80 students from the sathyamangalam and coimbatore area prof janani srree murallidharan introduced the students to the basics of cfd and also mapped it to openfoam and its use as a continuum mechanics and computational fluid dynamics tool swethamaniansridhar wed 1292020 1208 thursday december 12 2019 1200 events  ',	0),
(252,	'und',	'node_search',	' honorarium honorarium the fossee project has restarted the honorarium payment for textbook companion lab migration and the niche software activities like flowsheeting project circuit simulation project case study project etc the honorarium amount shall range from 1500 5000 1000 in case of complex problems inr as per the activity and the complexity of the work contributed we shall continue to issue the ecertificate and give credits on our website for the contributions made this policy will be effective for proposals accepted from jan 2024 please note that the fossee project may change this policy in the future sashirekha tue 3242020 1832  ',	0),
(253,	'und',	'node_search',	' workshop workshop oneday workshops on openfoam the cfd group at fossee iit bombay aims to promote the use of free libre and open source cfd toolbox openfoam free libre and open source field operation and manipulation which is a replacement for commercial packages like fluent and star ccm we have conducted oneday workshops that are useful to both new users and existing users wishing to broaden their basic knowledge of openfoam we have conducted workshops at shri guru gobind singhji institute of engineering and technology nanded maharashtra symbiosis institute of information technology pune vjti mumbai iit bombay mumbai ashleymelvin thu 3262020 1714 friday june 16 2017 1200 events  ',	0),
(254,	'und',	'node_search',	' lab migration forms lab migration forms the faculty in charge of the lab has to submit the lab proposal and provide his her contact details students solution provider should not send the lab proposal we require contact details of the professor and not the student all forms should have revenue stamps affixed on them please sign on the revenue stamps for colleges based in karnataka please mail the forms without the revenue stamps lab migration application form undertaking form teacher undertaking form hod undertaking form principal receipt copyright transfer form bank details form for any help please contact us sashirekha mon 3302020 1022  ',	0),
(255,	'und',	'node_search',	' advanced workshop on multiphase flows using openfoam september 2020 advanced workshop on multiphase flows using openfoam september 2020 advanced workshop on multiphase flows using openfoam conducted online in september 2020 cfdfossee team successfully conducted one of the first online advanced workshops on multiphase flows using openfoam it was actually a 1week workshop where the participants had to work on a screening task for 5 days and once selected they participated in the interactive session with other participants they were introduced to the vof volume of fluids method and eulerian methods in a demonstration and handson session conducted by the cfd team faculty from iit bombay s mechanical engineering department and department of energy science and engineering gave the theory behind the methods in their lectures and interacted with the participants during the workshop the participants presented their work from the screening task and later shared their experience and how immensely helpful the workshop was towards the end of the workshop the participants also interacted with an industry professional and learned the applications of openfoam in the real world it was truly a successful workshop encompassing all the gamuts of multiphase flow in openfoam swethamaniansridhar thu 11052020 1303 saturday september 19 2020 1200 events  ',	0),
(256,	'und',	'node_search',	' beginners workshop conducted online in september 2020 beginners workshop conducted online in september 2020 openfoam beginners workshop conducted online in september 2020 131 engineers were trained by cfd fossee iit bombay the workshop was conducted in a unique manner by breaking out into various classrooms each classroom session was conducted by 2 tas who used openfoam 7 spoken tutorial series to conduct the workshop prof janani srree murallidharan introduced the participants to the basics of cfd and openfoam and also helped them understand the underlying physics behind each problem the workshop helped the participants to switch from windows to linux os and from a commercial cfd software to openfoam they learned the basics of openfoam and committed to using opensource software in their research projects swethamaniansridhar fri 11062020 1246 saturday september 26 2020 1200 events  ',	0),
(257,	'und',	'node_search',	' sahil kukian testimonial sahil kukian testimonial swethamaniansridhar mon 6142021 1002 from fossee summer fellowship to an internship my journey with openfoam started with the spoken tutorial programme by the fossee team due to the nature of opensource software documentation and tutorials sometimes finding the right tutorials that explain the basics is very difficult but with the help of spoken tutorials i was able to easily grasp the workings of openfoam and learn my way upto to more complex problemsthis also helped me during the task phase for the fossee fellowship 2020 as i developed a good understanding of the basics in openfoam i was successfully able to complete the screening task phase and get selected for the fellowship during the fellowship professor janani srree swetha and the rest of the fossee team were incredible in their support and guidance even though in 2020 we were faced with lockdowns the fellowship was conducted through online modes and this did not take away from the fantastic experience and the knowledge that was gained while doing the projects i would also like to thank my mentors ashley melvin divyesh variya for their constant support professor janani had some very interesting projects for us related to covid19 specific research that could be performed using openfoam specifically in multiphase solvers such as twophaseeulerfoam later i also got the opportunity to test my knowledge that i gained in openfoam by acting as a teaching assistant ta in one of the workshops conducted by fossee a company called ufi filters had approached prof janani for an intern to work in openfoam and i was recommended by her i am currently working with them to solve complex flow problems using openfoam so overall the fossee fellowship has led to a very successful and fulfilling outcome regards sahil deepak kukian yes  ',	0),
(258,	'und',	'node_search',	' research migration project research migration project research migration project is an initiative that looks to promote and facilitate the usage of open source tools for cfd design and analysis specifically it looks to create a large resource database of research problems solved using openfoam to build this database we invite and encourage contributions from research scholars students and faculty members from various colleges involved in cfd related study to contribute to this database the researcher can choose a feasible cfd problem solved using a commercial cfd code and published in any leading journal paper or conference proceedings and solve the same using openfoam once it passes through our quality checks it will become part of this common database of research migration examples to ensure that your efforts are recognized and will benefit your career an approved research migration will be provided with an ecertificate technical requirements any student ug pg research scholars etc who has basic knowledge of computational fluid dynamics and openfoam  you may learn about openfoam using the spoken tutorials on openfoam  research migration project aims to only post studies that are reworked and reproduced in openfoam any feasible cfd study published in a journal paper or conference proceedings  and solved using commercial cfd software inhouse codes can be used for this purpose please refer to the completed research migration projects for a better understanding of what constitutes a research migration ashleymelvin tue 11232021 1319  ',	0),
(259,	'und',	'node_search',	' procedure procedure create a fossee cfd account and log in to the website to create an account click here  prepare a 1page synopsis describing the cfd problem statement and the research paper from which the problem statement is taken make sure your proposal is not in the list under completed research migration  and research migrations in progress  to view a sample synopsis click here  fill and submit the research migration proposal form  once your proposal is submitted it will be reviewed and approved disapproved after receiving the approval of your proposal you can proceed to complete the research migration project follow the submission guidelines carefully submit the completed research migration project directory in the submission portal  after receiving the approval of your proposal you may fill and send the required forms  to view the forms click here  for any further queries contact us at contactcfd fosseein ashleymelvin fri 11262021 1638  ',	0),
(260,	'und',	'node_search',	' submission guidelines submission guidelines abstract prepare a 1page synopsis describing the problem statement in a pdf format make sure that your proposal is not among the list of completed research migration projects or research migration projects in progress  along with the problem statement the synopsis should include details about the journal publication from which your work is being migrated this includes  title of the paper name of the journal publication author s  chapter volume pages to view a sample synopsis click here  research migration project directory prepare a research migration project director y in a zip tar or gz folder the directory should contain   mesh file that can be created using openfoam utilities or imported from other meshing software gmsh salome ansys etc  simulated case directories using openfoam v6 or above openfoam v1806 or above or foamextend 40 or above contours plots and data files postprocessed using paraview and or python scripts minimum 3page report of research migration project in pdf format specifying software details and dependencies on other codes functions if any for report format please refer to report template and guidelines  the editable templates microsoft word latex can be found here  the completed research migration project will be evaluated on the complexity of the project validated results using other sources references quality of the report ashleymelvin fri 11262021 1641  ',	0),
(261,	'und',	'node_search',	' research migration forms research migration forms download the following forms related to the research migration project these forms are to be filled and should be sent to the address given at the bottom of this page  please send all the forms in a single envelope forms not sent together shall not be considered under any circumstances   research migration project form copyright transfer form receipt form bank details form the mailing address for these forms is  prof janani srree murallidharan  mechanical engineering department  iit bombay powai mumbai 400076  please write  openfoam research migration project  on top of the envelope for the queries related to the submission of forms please contact contactcfd fosseein  ashleymelvin fri 11262021 1742  ',	0),
(262,	'und',	'node_search',	' honorarium honorarium the fossee project has restarted the honorarium payment for textbook companion lab migration and the niche software activities like flowsheeting project circuit simulation project case study project etc the honorarium amount shall range from 1500 5000 inr as per the activity and the complexity of the work contributed we shall continue to issue the ecertificate and give credits on our website for the contributions made this policy will be effective for proposals accepted from jan 2024 please note that the fossee project may change this policy in the future 5000 1000 in case of complex problems ashleymelvin fri 11262021 1744  ',	0),
(263,	'und',	'node_search',	' terms and conditions terms and conditions terms and conditions research migration project directory should contain mesh file simulated case directories contours plots and data files and a minimum 3page report complete the project in 1 month s time use only openfoam and other related free libre and open source software if required we cannot provide an honorarium certificate till we receive the forms  saketh tue 1042022 1044  ',	0),
(264,	'und',	'node_search',	' fossee summer fellowship 2023 fossee summer fellowship 2023 please keep visiting this page for updates last updated on 24 march 2023 the fossee summer fellowship 2023 will tentatively be offered physically onsite the fossee team will contact the selected candidates through emails registration and important dates  the link for registration and important dates are available here  screening tasks links  please select your screening task as per the choice filled while registering for the summer fellowship openfoam openfoam gui openfoam screening task openfoam gui screening task resources to learn openfoam  start learning openfoam using the spoken tutorials on openfoam  to learn more about openfoam please refer to the openfoam user guide  refer to the completed case studies to get a fair idea about the case study project refer to the completed research migration to get a fair idea about the research migration project screening task for the openfoam project  participants are requested to perform the task independently  and any form of copying is strongly discouraged stringent plagiarism checks will be done at fossee iit bombay and any malpractice found will result in disqualification  selections for the fellowship will be based on your performance in this task the decision of the fossee selection team will be final for any further queries write to us at contactcfd fosseein  with the subject line  fossee summer fellowship 2023   note  a candidate must complete the screening task to be eligible for the fellowship openfoam gui  screening task for the openfoam gui project  the cfdfossee team is developing a gui application to conveniently generate openfoam cases for details regarding resources and screening task for the fossee summer fellowship on openfoam gui project please click here  benefits of fellowship  opportunity to work with openfoamcfd experts in fossee certificate of fossee summer fellowship 2023 opportunity to work with professors in